WEBVTT

00:00:00.580 --> 00:00:04.550
You guys seem to be having fun.
That's good, I like it.

00:00:04.550 --> 00:00:08.570
And so, to Earphones, here's a present from me.

00:00:08.570 --> 00:00:11.930
What?! Debut song?!

00:01:45.820 --> 00:01:48.400
Are we really going to put out a CD?

00:01:48.400 --> 00:01:51.780
What are you saying? You were
interviewed about it already, weren't you?

00:01:51.780 --> 00:01:53.950
Earphones has already begun!

00:01:53.950 --> 00:01:56.660
In Bodhisattvon terms,
you're already past the Unveiling!

00:01:56.660 --> 00:01:59.050
The Un-veil-ing!

00:02:00.400 --> 00:02:01.880
CD...

00:02:01.880 --> 00:02:03.060
Debut!

00:02:03.460 --> 00:02:05.460
We're recording this weekend!

00:02:05.460 --> 00:02:09.760
Until then, make sure you listen to the
temporary track and practice your parts!

00:02:09.760 --> 00:02:10.400
Okay...

00:02:10.890 --> 00:02:11.940
That soon...?

00:02:12.600 --> 00:02:13.520
Okay!

00:02:13.520 --> 00:02:14.930
After recording,

00:02:14.930 --> 00:02:17.860
you'll film the PV and do the album cover photoshoot the following week.

00:02:17.860 --> 00:02:21.150
We have a dance teacher coming up
with the choreography right now,

00:02:21.150 --> 00:02:24.360
and of course, you'll have to master
it before we film the PV.

00:02:24.360 --> 00:02:24.910
Huh?

00:02:24.910 --> 00:02:29.150
Also, your debut single will be coming
out at the end of August at the latest.

00:02:29.150 --> 00:02:33.570
Because people definitely buy
more CDs during summer vacation!

00:02:33.570 --> 00:02:35.700
We'll do an event to
commemorate its release, too.

00:02:35.700 --> 00:02:37.040
I wonder where'll be good...?

00:02:37.040 --> 00:02:40.460
We'll decide on the date and
location soon and contact your agencies,

00:02:40.460 --> 00:02:42.140
so ask your managers.

00:02:42.140 --> 00:02:44.390
And so, I'm counting on you!

00:02:44.390 --> 00:02:46.710
Choreography...? Filming the music video...?

00:02:46.710 --> 00:02:49.260
We have to make sure we memorize
the lyrics and the dance moves!

00:02:49.260 --> 00:02:50.600
There's so much to do!

00:02:50.600 --> 00:02:56.110
Now, things are gonna get busy...
Oh, I forgot to tell you the title!

00:02:56.110 --> 00:02:57.100
Title?

00:02:57.100 --> 00:02:58.220
Of the song?

00:02:58.220 --> 00:02:59.650
What's the title?

00:03:00.230 --> 00:03:04.160
The title of the Earphones
debut single that I thought of is...

00:03:06.160 --> 00:03:08.740
The title is...

00:03:08.740 --> 00:03:12.170
"Into Your Ears"!

00:03:15.410 --> 00:03:17.490
I think it's a good title!

00:03:18.170 --> 00:03:19.810
Right?

00:03:23.080 --> 00:03:24.680
Singing and dancing...

00:03:24.680 --> 00:03:27.040
I wonder if I can do it...?

00:03:27.710 --> 00:03:30.880
No, I'll definitely show them I can!

00:03:30.880 --> 00:03:36.220
I'd like to tell the jobless me from last year
that I would have a chance like this!

00:03:36.220 --> 00:03:38.940
Oh, it wasn't that I didn't have anything.

00:03:39.670 --> 00:03:42.180
I recorded for a drama CD.

00:03:42.180 --> 00:03:44.320
It was my first drama CD.

00:03:45.560 --> 00:03:51.160
Okay, we'll start recording for
the <i>SPIRAL CAFÉ</i> drama CD now.

00:03:51.740 --> 00:03:54.780
First, we have Kugimiya Rie-san,
who will play Aretha.

00:03:54.780 --> 00:03:58.530
I'm Kugimiya Rie. Look forward
to working with you today.

00:03:58.530 --> 00:04:00.870
Looking forward to it.

00:04:00.870 --> 00:04:04.540
And then we have Ichinose Futaba-san playing Uma.

00:04:05.210 --> 00:04:06.250
lchinose-san!

00:04:06.250 --> 00:04:10.460
R-R-Right! I am Ichinose Futaba
from Aozora Production.

00:04:10.460 --> 00:04:12.190
I look forward to working with you today!

00:04:12.190 --> 00:04:14.380
Looking forward to it.

00:04:15.550 --> 00:04:18.070
Okay, let's start the dry run.

00:04:18.070 --> 00:04:20.210
Please do.

00:04:20.810 --> 00:04:25.520
A drama CD recording is
basically the same as an anime,

00:04:25.520 --> 00:04:27.900
but there's no video on the monitors,

00:04:27.900 --> 00:04:32.410
so it's a job that tests the actors'
imagination and acting abilities-koro.

00:04:34.220 --> 00:04:35.240
Ichinose-san.

00:04:35.240 --> 00:04:36.910
Huh? Yes?

00:04:37.410 --> 00:04:40.580
We have a line where we say
the same thing at the same time,

00:04:40.580 --> 00:04:43.200
so let's use the same mic for that.

00:04:43.200 --> 00:04:45.550
O-Okay, thank you!

00:04:47.430 --> 00:04:49.420
l-l'll do my best!

00:04:49.420 --> 00:04:52.000
l'll give the signal,
so let's do it together, okay?

00:04:52.000 --> 00:04:52.950
Okay.

00:04:54.670 --> 00:04:57.590
Then, are you saying we're the perpetrators?

00:04:57.590 --> 00:04:59.760
Yes, that's right.

00:04:59.760 --> 00:05:01.190
Do you have any evidence?

00:05:01.190 --> 00:05:04.570
This is Kilimanjaro
masquerading as Blue Mountain.

00:05:04.570 --> 00:05:07.520
Uma, bring the beans
from the scene of the crime.

00:05:07.520 --> 00:05:11.230
All right! Onee-sama, here they are.

00:05:11.230 --> 00:05:12.140
What? No way...

00:05:12.140 --> 00:05:13.540
K-Kugimiya-san is so close!
What? No way...

00:05:13.540 --> 00:05:14.440
K-Kugimiya-san is so close!

00:05:14.440 --> 00:05:17.740
And she smells good...

00:05:22.300 --> 00:05:25.830
With this, the trip is over!

00:05:25.830 --> 00:05:27.340
Okay, good.

00:05:29.420 --> 00:05:32.140
Kugimiya-san was wonderful.

00:05:33.590 --> 00:05:37.140
She was really nice to me
even though I was a super newbie.

00:05:37.140 --> 00:05:39.800
I wish we could work together again,

00:05:39.800 --> 00:05:44.260
but I have to work hard so I can be
in many different kinds of shows.

00:05:44.260 --> 00:05:46.270
All right, I'm going to do it!

00:05:47.410 --> 00:05:48.070
What?!

00:05:52.420 --> 00:05:54.120
An anime?!

00:05:55.780 --> 00:05:56.500
This please!

00:05:56.500 --> 00:05:57.780
R-Right!

00:06:00.840 --> 00:06:03.840
Which? Which should I start with?

00:06:03.840 --> 00:06:06.910
Wh-What's with this big wave of work?!

00:06:06.910 --> 00:06:08.460
Futaba-san, calm down-koro!

00:06:08.460 --> 00:06:10.470
Neither the manga nor the CD will run away-koro.

00:06:10.470 --> 00:06:13.040
Y-You're right.

00:06:17.710 --> 00:06:19.980
First, check the news.

00:06:19.980 --> 00:06:21.220
Hm?

00:06:21.220 --> 00:06:22.730
Just this, huh?

00:06:23.220 --> 00:06:28.740
They often just say there will be an
anime first to warm up the fans' expectations-koro.

00:06:28.740 --> 00:06:31.740
Right. I'll need to check
the magazine from now on, too.

00:06:33.520 --> 00:06:35.810
I'll get to see Kugimiya-san again, huh?

00:06:37.150 --> 00:06:38.500
I'm so happy...

00:06:39.110 --> 00:06:42.420
It'll be nice if she thinks
you've improved, huh-koro?

00:06:46.120 --> 00:06:49.300
Right, right, you mustn't
forget about Earphones-koro!

00:06:54.500 --> 00:06:56.930
I'm going to sing this!

00:07:01.060 --> 00:07:03.560
Yes... Yes...

00:07:03.560 --> 00:07:06.800
Oh, right. Thank you for your call.

00:07:07.600 --> 00:07:09.560
Hello, Ichinose-san?

00:07:09.560 --> 00:07:10.730
This is Konno.

00:07:10.730 --> 00:07:13.070
The date of your choreography
lesson has been decided.

00:07:13.070 --> 00:07:15.400
Oh, right. At 4 p.m., right? Okay.

00:07:15.400 --> 00:07:17.730
Thank you for letting me know.

00:07:17.730 --> 00:07:20.190
Oh, um, Konno-san, uh...

00:07:20.190 --> 00:07:20.820
Yes?

00:07:20.820 --> 00:07:24.200
Have there been any other calls, or offers...

00:07:24.200 --> 00:07:25.590
Anything like that come for me?

00:07:25.910 --> 00:07:28.240
Huh? No, there haven't...

00:07:28.580 --> 00:07:30.540
Is that right?

00:07:30.540 --> 00:07:31.750
Is there something...?

00:07:31.750 --> 00:07:33.890
We will start recording soon!

00:07:33.890 --> 00:07:37.380
It's nothing! S-Sorry, thanks for your call!

00:07:37.380 --> 00:07:38.740
Goodbye!

00:07:39.590 --> 00:07:40.620
I'll be right there!

00:08:04.200 --> 00:08:05.410
All right!

00:08:05.910 --> 00:08:10.040
I wonder if <i>SPIRAL CAFÉ</i> will contact me soon.

00:08:10.040 --> 00:08:14.840
If it starts in January, then we'll start
recording in October or November...

00:08:15.250 --> 00:08:18.960
Oh right, I'll be busier with this
and the work for Earphones,

00:08:18.960 --> 00:08:22.340
so I should talk to the
manager at my part-time job.

00:08:22.340 --> 00:08:24.600
Oh, no! It's past 11 p.m.!

00:08:24.600 --> 00:08:26.260
That's right! I have to go to sleep!

00:08:26.260 --> 00:08:28.390
Lack of sleep is the archenemy of your throat!

00:08:28.390 --> 00:08:31.970
Oh, I should turn down the AC!
Where's the remote...?

00:08:31.970 --> 00:08:35.610
Also, a senpai told me
I should sleep with a facemask on...

00:08:37.020 --> 00:08:38.740
One! Two!

00:08:38.740 --> 00:08:40.610
Right, right!

00:08:40.610 --> 00:08:42.620
Left, left!

00:08:42.620 --> 00:08:44.990
Come on, smile more!

00:08:44.990 --> 00:08:46.750
More energy!

00:08:50.380 --> 00:08:54.560
Okay! Passion! More! Feel it!

00:08:56.540 --> 00:08:59.000
Okay, that's it for the lesson.

00:08:59.000 --> 00:08:59.710
Huh?

00:08:59.710 --> 00:09:01.220
We can still keep going, though!

00:09:01.800 --> 00:09:08.430
I have to go to another job.
Practice on your own with the DVD after this!

00:09:08.430 --> 00:09:09.220
Huh?

00:09:09.220 --> 00:09:09.890
That's...

00:09:09.890 --> 00:09:11.680
Seriously?

00:09:11.680 --> 00:09:18.350
In times like this, it's rare for a teacher to
make sure you can do everything perfectly-koro.

00:09:18.350 --> 00:09:20.990
You just have to work
hard on your own after this-koro!

00:09:21.240 --> 00:09:23.730
Okay, work hard!

00:09:25.900 --> 00:09:29.540
I... thought I could dance
a little better than that...

00:09:29.540 --> 00:09:32.000
It's amazing how bad you are at dancing, Futaba.

00:09:33.160 --> 00:09:38.210
Um, would you like to
practice together, the three of us?

00:09:38.210 --> 00:09:42.600
Yeah... Even if we practice on our own,
it's hard to tell where to stand by ourselves.

00:09:42.600 --> 00:09:44.460
Let's decide on a date!

00:09:44.880 --> 00:09:47.050
Do you have time for that, lchigo?

00:09:47.050 --> 00:09:50.890
Huh? Well, I'm busy,
but I'll make time somehow...

00:09:50.890 --> 00:09:56.480
Yeah, I'm sure you're all busy,
but let's work hard together!

00:09:56.480 --> 00:09:57.980
Yeah.

00:09:58.850 --> 00:10:01.400
I mean, we actually got this chance!

00:10:03.150 --> 00:10:04.830
Good morning!

00:10:04.830 --> 00:10:06.940
We've decided on a
release date for the new song,

00:10:06.940 --> 00:10:08.830
so please announce it at the end of the show.

00:10:08.830 --> 00:10:10.660
Here's the information.

00:10:10.660 --> 00:10:13.700
You can decide how you want
to split up the lines. Thanks.

00:10:13.700 --> 00:10:14.720
Got it.

00:10:16.910 --> 00:10:20.870
Okay, I'll set it up,
and then Rin-chan, you explain it.

00:10:20.870 --> 00:10:22.130
Okay!

00:10:22.130 --> 00:10:25.590
And then, Futaba, will you say
something funny and close us out?

00:10:25.590 --> 00:10:27.520
Something funny?

00:10:27.520 --> 00:10:30.970
You can just talk normally, and it'll
turn into something funny. You'll be fine!

00:10:30.970 --> 00:10:32.590
That doesn't sound like a compliment!

00:10:32.590 --> 00:10:34.430
Oh, excuse me for a moment.

00:10:34.430 --> 00:10:35.600
Oh, sure.

00:10:35.600 --> 00:10:36.520
Sure.

00:10:36.520 --> 00:10:39.520
Hey, Futaba, did you try dancing to the music?

00:10:39.520 --> 00:10:40.990
No, not yet...

00:10:40.990 --> 00:10:45.270
It's pretty bad! It's super hard
trying to dance in time with the music!

00:10:45.270 --> 00:10:46.570
Oh, no... What should I do...?

00:10:46.570 --> 00:10:49.000
Futaba, make sure you remember all the moves!

00:10:51.740 --> 00:10:53.160
Are you listening?

00:10:53.160 --> 00:10:55.240
You need to work on your
dancing the most, Futaba!

00:10:55.240 --> 00:10:57.010
Uh, right...

00:10:58.260 --> 00:11:03.260
Now,we have a gorgeous announcement
for all the subjects of Planet Strawberry!

00:11:03.260 --> 00:11:05.170
What? I wonder if it's gorgeous?

00:11:05.170 --> 00:11:07.520
Even if it's a lie,
we should still call it "gorgeous"!

00:11:07.520 --> 00:11:09.970
You said it's a lie...

00:11:09.970 --> 00:11:13.050
It's fine, just give the subjects
the royal decree, Rin-Rin!

00:11:13.050 --> 00:11:18.240
Okay. Um, it's been decided that we,
Earphones, will release a debut single!

00:11:18.240 --> 00:11:19.980
Yay!

00:11:19.980 --> 00:11:21.640
Our dream is to have a U.S. tour!

00:11:21.640 --> 00:11:23.100
That's an exaggeration.

00:11:23.100 --> 00:11:24.740
Even if it's a lie, you should exaggerate!

00:11:24.740 --> 00:11:26.730
It's a really good song!

00:11:26.730 --> 00:11:29.750
Look forward to it,
citizens of Planet Strawberry!

00:11:31.820 --> 00:11:35.030
Also, is it all right if I
make another announcement?

00:11:35.030 --> 00:11:36.500
Hm? Go ahead.

00:11:36.500 --> 00:11:41.410
Um, this is just for me, Kohana Rin...

00:11:41.720 --> 00:11:45.560
The manga currently being serialized in <i>Weekly Shonen Zunder</i>,

00:11:45.560 --> 00:11:49.520
<i>SPIRAL CAFÉ,</i> will have an anime starting January.

00:11:49.520 --> 00:11:52.400
I will be playing the role of Uma.

00:11:53.560 --> 00:11:54.840
What, you're promoting something?

00:11:54.840 --> 00:11:59.890
Sorry! The producer of
the show told me to do it.

00:11:59.890 --> 00:12:03.140
I think it'll be a good show, so please watch!

00:12:03.140 --> 00:12:04.270
That's what she says.

00:12:04.270 --> 00:12:06.770
Oh, don't be mad at me!

00:12:06.770 --> 00:12:08.060
I'm just kidding!

00:12:08.060 --> 00:12:09.650
Well, what's the story about?

00:12:09.650 --> 00:12:13.700
Um, there's a café that's
also a detective agency,

00:12:13.700 --> 00:12:18.090
and the owner solves cases
that are a little mysterious.

00:12:18.090 --> 00:12:22.410
I play the little sister of the
secretary played by Kugimiya Rie-san!

00:12:23.180 --> 00:12:24.750
Wow, Kugimiya-san?!

00:12:24.750 --> 00:12:27.040
I want to work with her sometime, too!

00:12:27.040 --> 00:12:29.590
I'm looking forward to it, as well!

00:12:29.590 --> 00:12:30.750
Hm?

00:12:30.750 --> 00:12:32.460
Futa-Futa?

00:12:34.220 --> 00:12:36.680
P-Please look forward to it!

00:12:36.680 --> 00:12:38.140
Don't tell me you were sleeping?

00:12:38.140 --> 00:12:40.560
You weren't listening to what I was saying?

00:12:40.560 --> 00:12:44.980
Oh, sorry, sorry! I was just thinking
about what to eat for dinner...

00:12:44.980 --> 00:12:47.560
Jeez, in the middle of recording?

00:12:47.560 --> 00:12:49.490
I like fermented <i>natto</i> beans!

00:12:49.490 --> 00:12:52.410
No way, there's no <i>natto</i> on Planet Strawberry!

00:12:52.410 --> 00:12:54.820
But at the supermarket the other day...

00:12:59.910 --> 00:13:02.590
The weather forecast said it would be sunny...

00:13:04.290 --> 00:13:05.630
There's thunder, huh?

00:13:06.080 --> 00:13:07.830
Wanna wait out the rain somewhere?

00:13:07.830 --> 00:13:10.380
That sounds good! Let's go to a nearby café-

00:13:10.380 --> 00:13:11.600
l'm going to go home today!

00:13:11.600 --> 00:13:12.310
Huh?
l'm going to go home today!

00:13:58.630 --> 00:14:00.980
Um, this character is...

00:14:00.980 --> 00:14:01.640
Detective SPIRAL CAFÉ
Um, this character is...

00:14:01.640 --> 00:14:01.880
Detective SPIRAL CAFÉ

00:14:02.810 --> 00:14:05.650
Oh, there was a drama CD!

00:14:06.810 --> 00:14:12.660
Oh? The main cast looks
the same as the anime...

00:14:15.430 --> 00:14:16.910
Ichigo

00:14:18.360 --> 00:14:21.260
Hello, Rin-chan? Can you talk now?

00:14:21.880 --> 00:14:24.420
Is something wrong? You seem down.

00:14:24.420 --> 00:14:26.670
Th-That's not true!

00:14:26.940 --> 00:14:32.540
I hope not. Yeah, just checking what
time we're practicing. It's at 5 p.m., right?

00:14:32.540 --> 00:14:34.090
What? It's at 7 p.m.?!

00:14:34.090 --> 00:14:35.930
Shoot, I got mixed up.

00:14:36.200 --> 00:14:37.840
I wonder if Futaba's okay.

00:14:37.840 --> 00:14:38.690
Huh....?

00:14:38.690 --> 00:14:40.970
I called her earlier, but she didn't pick up.

00:14:40.970 --> 00:14:42.550
Maybe she's at her part-time job.

00:14:42.550 --> 00:14:44.400
l texted her, though...

00:14:48.520 --> 00:14:50.940
Rin-chan seemed kind of down...

00:14:50.940 --> 00:14:53.770
And Futaba hasn't called me back yet, either...

00:14:54.700 --> 00:14:58.690
They must be worried about
filming the PV after all.

00:14:58.690 --> 00:14:59.730
It's not surprising.

00:15:00.490 --> 00:15:05.200
Next to a perfect entertainer
named Moesaki Ichigo,

00:15:05.200 --> 00:15:07.700
it's only natural to feel inferior!

00:15:09.640 --> 00:15:13.710
Well, this is where
I've gotta support those two!

00:15:21.820 --> 00:15:23.260
Oh, Rin-chan.

00:15:23.260 --> 00:15:27.010
Oh, good morning. Where's Futaba-san?

00:15:27.010 --> 00:15:28.890
She's not here yet.

00:15:31.120 --> 00:15:31.760
It's Futaba.

00:15:34.020 --> 00:15:39.790
"Sorry. Work came up suddenly,
so I cannot make it today."

00:15:43.580 --> 00:15:45.200
Good morning.

00:15:45.200 --> 00:15:48.790
Morning. Oh? lchinose, you're off today?

00:15:48.790 --> 00:15:51.180
Um, yes, that's right.

00:15:51.180 --> 00:15:52.340
Good morning!

00:15:52.790 --> 00:15:56.790
Um, I received a call about a job-

00:15:56.790 --> 00:15:58.630
Yes, congratulations.

00:15:58.630 --> 00:16:00.760
Will you talk to the
receptionist about the details?

00:16:00.760 --> 00:16:01.730
Yes!

00:16:01.730 --> 00:16:05.760
Oh, the cast list was sent over.
And here's the proposal.

00:16:05.760 --> 00:16:07.100
Please look over them.

00:16:07.100 --> 00:16:09.010
Okay, thank you!

00:16:09.010 --> 00:16:13.270
I love the manga this is based on!
I never thought I'd be chosen for it...

00:16:13.270 --> 00:16:14.620
Then you'll have to work extra hard, huh?

00:16:14.620 --> 00:16:14.980
Lucky...
Then you'll have to work extra hard, huh?

00:16:14.980 --> 00:16:15.490
Lucky...

00:16:16.520 --> 00:16:20.230
Why wasn't I chosen to be Uma?

00:16:20.230 --> 00:16:22.110
Because I was bad?

00:16:22.110 --> 00:16:23.750
Because I'm not popular?

00:16:23.750 --> 00:16:27.450
Because no one thought I was necessary...?

00:16:29.240 --> 00:16:32.010
No, I can't cry in a place like this...

00:16:40.440 --> 00:16:41.640
l'm sorry!

00:16:42.820 --> 00:16:43.890
Huh?

00:16:44.900 --> 00:16:45.650
Ow!

00:16:46.180 --> 00:16:47.420
Are you all right?

00:16:48.720 --> 00:16:52.470
We need all three of us
together to get a feel for it, huh?

00:16:55.640 --> 00:16:59.160
Does this happen often?

00:16:59.900 --> 00:17:02.910
I'm shocked, and it hurts.

00:17:04.150 --> 00:17:07.420
I don't know what to do anymore...

00:17:07.420 --> 00:17:13.410
Hmm... Yeah, if the production company
changes, or there are budget issues,

00:17:13.410 --> 00:17:19.180
the cast can often change
between the drama CD and the anime.

00:17:19.180 --> 00:17:23.180
On top of that, they never tell
you the changes ahead of time.

00:17:23.760 --> 00:17:27.430
It's painful, but it's
something all seiyuu experience.

00:17:30.060 --> 00:17:33.530
I... can't do it...

00:17:33.850 --> 00:17:36.030
You can't just say that...

00:17:36.320 --> 00:17:39.600
I don't know what face I should
make when I see her...

00:17:39.600 --> 00:17:43.740
How can I work with her
when it hurts this much...?

00:17:43.740 --> 00:17:44.540
I...

00:17:50.160 --> 00:17:58.290
You know, it doesn't matter to the
audience if you're depressed, or hurting.

00:17:58.290 --> 00:18:02.710
No matter what happens, you have to
do your work with everything you have.

00:18:02.710 --> 00:18:06.210
A family member might be in the hospital,

00:18:06.210 --> 00:18:08.600
or a pet might have died.

00:18:09.430 --> 00:18:13.760
But because it's work, no one
lets that show in their attitude.

00:18:13.760 --> 00:18:17.360
That's the least a seiyuu
can do to prepare for work.

00:18:17.360 --> 00:18:21.120
I think it would be rude to
your fellow seiyuu otherwise.

00:18:23.120 --> 00:18:26.870
To do what is expected
of you under any circumstance.

00:18:26.870 --> 00:18:28.380
That's what a professional does.

00:18:31.740 --> 00:18:37.380
I thought the work of a
seiyuu was more like a dream.

00:18:40.140 --> 00:18:41.890
The audience sees the dream.

00:18:43.300 --> 00:18:45.640
We show them that dream.

00:18:46.460 --> 00:18:50.650
That's what a seiyuu is. Right, Futa-Futa?

00:19:06.410 --> 00:19:09.370
<i>Detective SPIRAL CAFÉ</i> Drama CD vol. 1

00:19:12.240 --> 00:19:13.660
I was really bad...

00:19:13.660 --> 00:19:17.670
I thought I did a better job...

00:19:18.290 --> 00:19:21.800
Futaba-san, I've heard that being able
to tell how bad you were before

00:19:21.800 --> 00:19:25.180
means that's how much you've matured-koro.

00:19:26.840 --> 00:19:27.930
Yeah.

00:19:42.360 --> 00:19:43.450
Um... About <i>SPIRA-</i>

00:19:43.450 --> 00:19:46.490
The anime, <i>SPIRAL CAFÉ,</i>
that you're going to be in...

00:19:46.490 --> 00:19:48.700
I was in the drama CD for that.

00:19:50.280 --> 00:19:53.440
Honestly, I'm really jealous of you.

00:19:53.990 --> 00:19:55.450
I wanted to do it.

00:19:55.450 --> 00:19:59.460
U-Um... I...

00:19:59.870 --> 00:20:03.970
But... I want to hear what
your Uma sounds like, too!

00:20:03.970 --> 00:20:05.050
Huh?!

00:20:05.050 --> 00:20:08.680
I'm sure it'll be completely different...

00:20:08.680 --> 00:20:12.600
I'm jealous, and if I'm honest
with myself, I'm frustrated, too-

00:20:12.600 --> 00:20:14.770
So much that it's making me grind my teeth...

00:20:14.770 --> 00:20:19.780
But I'm looking forward to it.
And that's the truth!

00:20:22.540 --> 00:20:26.140
I'm sorry... I don't know what to say...

00:20:27.080 --> 00:20:30.830
This is where you should say, "I'll do my best!"

00:20:33.580 --> 00:20:37.250
Yes! I'll do my best as Uma!

00:20:38.000 --> 00:20:39.460
Ta-da!

00:20:39.460 --> 00:20:41.970
You two don't have
enough strawberries, huh?

00:20:41.970 --> 00:20:45.380
Once we finish filming the
PV, I'll let you eat this!

00:20:45.380 --> 00:20:47.090
Aren't you more motivated now?

00:20:47.090 --> 00:20:49.920
Isn't it considerate of the strawberry princess?

00:20:49.920 --> 00:20:53.680
What would you two do without me?

00:20:54.100 --> 00:20:59.320
So that happened, and I was touched
by out-of-character adolescence...

00:20:59.320 --> 00:21:04.590
I see... I remember that girl...

00:21:04.590 --> 00:21:06.320
We're about to start!

00:21:06.320 --> 00:21:07.320
Okay!

00:21:08.280 --> 00:21:11.150
She'll be fine. It's something
everyone has to overcome!

00:21:11.150 --> 00:21:12.480
That's true.

00:21:16.360 --> 00:21:20.910
This will probably keep happening from now on.

00:21:20.910 --> 00:21:26.840
But I can't let my frustration
get the best of me. I'm sure of that.

00:21:28.800 --> 00:21:31.300
Okay, we're done for today!

00:21:32.800 --> 00:21:40.560
And so, I think the PV for Earphones' debut song, "Into Your Ears," will be really good!

00:21:40.560 --> 00:21:44.650
On sale August 27. Please look forward to it!

00:21:44.650 --> 00:21:47.610
We'll let you know more details
once we have more information!

00:21:47.610 --> 00:21:50.030
See you next week!

00:21:52.570 --> 00:21:54.070
Good work!

00:21:54.070 --> 00:21:55.640
Good work today!I

00:21:55.640 --> 00:21:56.120
Yeah!

00:21:56.620 --> 00:21:59.880
Actually, about your debut song-

00:21:59.880 --> 00:22:00.880
Yes?

00:22:00.880 --> 00:22:05.150
Sorry, but it looks like it'll be impossible
to get it out by the end of August.

00:22:05.150 --> 00:22:06.880
Huh?

00:22:06.880 --> 00:22:09.930
Huh?!
